<a id="устранение-сопутствующей-проблемы-fixer"></a>

# Resolve an incidental problem (Fixer)

Use this route when a separate environment, tool or process problem stops the task. Fix defects in the task result through normal work. Fixer is a procedure; it needs no separate skill, permanent role or mandatory subagent. Use a specialist when independent diagnosis is worth the context handoff cost.

1. Record the original action and observed error without secrets. Check how the failure relates to the task and which actions are already authorized. Do not expand authority to restore the environment.
2. If the project has an issue registry, search `issue-list` by symptom and tags, then read a suitable record. Compare environment, conditions, current verification and solution consequences. Matching text does not establish the cause. Treat a stale record as a hypothesis.
3. Diagnose and fix the minimum within authority. A material requirement change uses task/spec. If authority is missing, continue independent work and request only the needed decision. Do not run record recipes automatically.
4. Repeat the original blocked action. Success confirms restoration in tested conditions; a claim that the cause is removed needs separate grounds. State an unknown cause honestly. Record temporary restoration as `mitigated`. Check changes by risk and the local matrix; no new full barrier or separate review for every record is required.
5. Save only reusable problems: repeated, costly to diagnose, nontrivial to solve or with an important limit. Typos and routine intermediate errors need no record. Search before creating one. Update conditions, confirmed cause, solution, prevention and links. Register the occurrence once through `issue-record`. Keep logs separately in the project location, with safe links from the record.
6. When cause and risk justify it, add prevention through a check, configuration or root-cause fix. Return to the first unfinished task action. Report the material remainder or issue link. An existing issue record owns reusable conditions, diagnosis and solution; the task keeps the link and impact on its result. Without a record, a task note is enough. The record does not replace requirements, task evidence or user authority.

The registry belongs to one project and is optional. Do not create it in advance. Recheck conditions and authority when moving a solution between projects. [Issue reference](../references/tools/issues.md) owns format, commands, states and recovery. Schema checks consistency; the executor assesses diagnosis truth and applicability.
